1
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:11,270
A news report says 65,000 fans watched a match.

2
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:15,430
The number is rounded to the nearest thousand.

3
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:18,870
What is the smallest the real crowd could have been?

4
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:22,390
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:27,860
64,500 is the smallest number that rounds up to 65,000.

6
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:32,490
Anything less would round down to 64,000.

7
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:40,620
The largest crowd is 65,499, because 65,500 would round up to 66,000.

8
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:45,110
Remember: 4.36 to 1 decimal place is 4.4.

9
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:49,380
2,450 to the nearest 100 is 2,500.

10
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:51,680
A rounded value stands for a range.

11
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:57,500
Go half a unit down for the lower bound, and half a unit up for the upper bound.

12
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:58,230
Your turn.

13
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,370
A length is 4.7 metres, to 1 decimal place.

14
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:03,130
What is its upper bound?

15
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:06,500
Pause the video and try it.

16
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:08,030
The unit is 0.1.

17
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,960
Half of 0.1 is 0.05.

18
00:01:10,010 --> 00:01:13,030
So the bounds are 4.65 and 4.75.

19
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:16,560
The upper bound is 4.75 metres.

20
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:19,050
Write the range as an inequality.

21
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:21,160
The lower bound is included.

22
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:26,170
The upper bound is not, because 4.75 would round up to 4.8.

23
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,490
Here is the method.

24
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:31,820
Step 1: find the accuracy: the unit it was rounded to.

25
00:01:31,870 --> 00:01:34,480
Step 2: halve that unit.

26
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:38,030
Step 3: lower bound is the value minus a half unit.

27
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:41,500
Upper bound is the value plus a half unit.

28
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:46,380
Step 4: write: lower, less than or equal to X, less than upper.

29
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:50,550
A time is 40 seconds, to the nearest 5 seconds.

30
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,060
Half of 5 is 2.5.

31
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:56,160
So the bounds are 37.5 and 42.5 seconds.

32
00:01:56,210 --> 00:01:56,940
Your turn.

33
00:01:56,990 --> 00:02:00,430
A mass is 320 grams, to the nearest 10 grams.

34
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:01,990
What are its bounds?

35
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:05,090
Pause and work it out.

36
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:06,530
Half of 10 is 5.

37
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:12,390
So the mass is at least 315 grams, and less than 325 grams.

38
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:16,410
A rope is 12 metres long, to the nearest metre.

39
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:19,060
Could it really be 12.6 metres?

40
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:21,540
The bounds are 11.5 and 12.5.

41
00:02:21,590 --> 00:02:24,140
12.6 is too long, so no.

42
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:27,360
A mass is 6.2 kilograms to 1 decimal place.

43
00:02:27,410 --> 00:02:29,000
Ana writes the bounds.

44
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,040
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:32,420
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:34,050
She used half of 1.

47
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:38,120
The unit is 0.1, and half of 0.1 is 0.05.

48
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:42,500
The bounds are 6.15 and 6.25 kilograms.

49
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:51,910
Engineers give tolerances, like 10 millimetres, plus or minus 0.05 millimetres, so that parts always fit together.

50
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,260
One last question.

51
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:55,820
A number is 90, to the nearest 10.

52
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,620
What is its lower bound?

53
00:02:57,670 --> 00:03:01,060
Pause the video and answer.

54
00:03:01,110 --> 00:03:02,830
Half of 10 is 5.

55
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,260
90 minus 5 is 85.

56
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:09,330
To remember: the bounds are half a unit either side.

57
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:13,440
Write lower, less than or equal to X, less than upper.

58
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:16,150
The upper bound itself rounds up.

59
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,800
Check the accuracy carefully.

60
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:23,910
Great work! Now practise lesson 3.4 on Camday.
